    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3663" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ărī^us</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arr-</span></b> ), i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρεῖος</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄριος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a renowned heretic</i>, also
			Ārĭus, <i><span class="en">Prud. Psych.
			794</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ărīānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>pertaining to
			Arius</i>, <i>Arian</i>, <i><span class="en">Hier.
				adv. Lucif. 7</span></i>.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ărīāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the followers of Arius</i>, <i>the Arians</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Hier. adv. Lucif. 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug.
				Haeres. 49</span></i>.</div>
